  "sdk_method": "steer",
  "sdk_response_type": "SteerResponse",
  "summary": "Steer a running turn",
  "description": "Send a new message to a turn that is already running, without losing what the agent is doing. This is what typing into a coding agent while it works does: the instruction is taken into account and the work continues.\n\nWhere the harness has a native mid-turn primitive (Claude Code, Codex, pi, Prime Agent) nothing is interrupted and the response has `native: true`. Where it does not (OpenCode), Boat interrupts that turn and immediately continues the SAME conversation with the instruction, keeping the session and its memory, and the response has `native: false`.\n\nRefused with **409 `no_running_turn`** when the conversation has nothing in flight; queue work with `POST /prompt` instead. The steer shows up in `GET /events` as a `steer` event. See [Integrated agents](/integrated-agents).",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "sandboxId",
      "in": "path",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Public Sandbox id returned by create/list/get sandbox calls.",
      "example_value": "sample"
    },
    {
      "name": "conversation",
      "in": "query",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Conversation id to steer. Also accepted in the body. Omit to steer the sandbox's most-recently-active conversation.",
      "example_value": "sample"
    }
  ],
